<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>. ValidationRule.Description is capped
        at 255 characters and the comment must sit INSIDE the root element - a comment placed
        ABOVE <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 1, ITEM 9 (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t1-design.md
        §3 Item 9, story 2's AC). Shape follows Account.Record_Type_Is_Immutable exactly,
        including its $Permission exemption pattern.

        =====================================================================================
        NOT(ISNEW()) + ISCHANGED(RecordTypeId) - MUST NOT FIRE ON CREATE.
        =====================================================================================
        DispositionService stamps the record type AT INSERT on both create paths
        (findOrCreate:323, initiateAndSubmit:445). NOT(ISNEW()) keeps this rule out of that path
        entirely; ISCHANGED(RecordTypeId) then means only a SUBSEQUENT change to an already-saved
        record can ever trip it.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 LOCK BOUNDARY - USER DECISION AT GATE 1, 2026-08-31, OVERRIDING THE DESIGN DOC'S OWN
        D-7 RECOMMENDATION. DO NOT "CORRECT" THIS BACK TO THE DESIGN DOC'S SHAPE.
        =====================================================================================
        The record type is changeable ONLY while Disposition_Stage__c = 'Disposition Readiness'.
        It is LOCKED from 'BOV Outreach' onward through 'Sale Closes', on BOTH record types. There
        is no 'BOV Outreach' exemption in the formula below, even though 'BOV Outreach' is (like
        'Disposition Readiness') a stage that precedes Broker Selection.

        agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t1-design.md's own D-7 row recommended a LOOSER
        boundary - free at both 'Disposition Readiness' AND 'BOV Outreach', locked only from
        'Broker Selection' onward. The user was asked this explicitly at Gate 1 and chose
        "lock as soon as the sale decision is approved" over that recommendation. THIS FILE
        IMPLEMENTS THE USER'S CHOICE, NOT THE DESIGN DOC'S. A future reader who opens the design
        doc and finds the looser rule recommended there should not conclude this file is wrong -
        the design doc records a recommendation that was NOT the one taken.

        WHY THIS BOUNDARY, IN THE USER'S OWN TERMS: a principal approves a specific disposition
        path at Approval #1 (Sale_Decision_Approval), and nothing downstream of THAT approval may
        change it. Sale_Decision_Approval's entry criterion is Disposition_Stage__c =
        'Disposition Readiness' - so "past Readiness" and "past the sale decision" are the SAME
        boundary. That is why the lock starts at 'BOV Outreach' and not one stage later: by the
        time a disposition reaches 'BOV Outreach' the sale-decision approval has already run, and
        the path it approved is meant to stick.

        CONSEQUENCE WORTH STATING: an OFF-MARKET disposition never passes through 'BOV Outreach'
        at all - that value is excluded from the Off_Market record type's Disposition_Stage__c
        set (Off_Market's sequence is Readiness, Broker Selection, NDA, Release Materials, Offer
        Selection, LOI, PSA, Closing, Sale Closes - see Disposition_Stage__c's own header). So the
        NOW-REMOVED 'BOV Outreach' exemption in the design doc's looser proposal would only ever
        have applied to ON-MARKET deals; an off-market disposition would already have locked one
        stage earlier than an on-market one under that looser rule. Under THIS boundary (locked
        from BOV Outreach) both record types behave IDENTICALLY: changeable at Readiness, locked
        from the very next stage onward, whatever that stage is called on either path.

        THE STAGE TEST IS STILL AN EXCLUSION LIST, NOT A RANK COMPARISON, AND THAT IS STILL
        DELIBERATE - the two record types have different stage sequences (On_Market 11 stages,
        Off_Market 9), so no single numeric stage index means the same thing on both paths. With
        only ONE free stage now, the exclusion list has shrunk to a single ISPICKVAL term, but the
        reasoning for using ISPICKVAL rather than an index is unchanged.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 $Permission MUST BE THE THREE-SEGMENT FORM: {!$Permission.<Name>}.
        =====================================================================================
        {!$CustomPermission.<Name>} is REJECTED by the Metadata API - measured on this project
        2026-08-12. Account.Record_Type_Is_Immutable's working spelling
        (NOT($Permission.Lead_Convert_Account_RecordType_Stamp)) is the template copied here
        verbatim in shape, substituting Disposition_Record_Type_Override.

        🔴 THIS RULE'S CUSTOM PERMISSION, customPermissions/Disposition_Record_Type_Override, MUST
        LAND IN THE SAME OR AN EARLIER DEPLOY THAN THIS FILE. If this rule deploys first, the
        merge field resolves to a permission that does not yet exist - which the platform accepts
        (it simply evaluates false, so nobody can override, rather than failing the deploy) but
        means the admin escape hatch does not function until the permission both exists AND is
        assigned via the consolidated permission-set pass.

        =====================================================================================
        errorDisplayField -> Disposition_Stage__c, matching the two sibling rules on this object
        (All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression, Wire_Complete_Before_Sale_Closes) which both anchor
        their error there rather than on the field that actually changed.
        =====================================================================================

        =====================================================================================
        ⚠ TWO SWEEPS OWED TO THE DEVELOPER AGENT, NOT PERFORMED BY THIS FILE.
        =====================================================================================
        1. Grep whether anything writes Disposition__c.RecordTypeId AFTER insert anywhere in the
           Apex codebase. Nothing was found in the paths read while designing this change, but
           the sweep itself is explicit developer scope (design doc §4).
        2. TestDataFactory.dispositionRecordTypeId DELIBERATELY DEGRADES TO NO RECORD TYPE when
           the type is absent or unavailable ("an undeployed record type must not turn every
           disposition test in the repo red"). A test that later tries to stamp a record type
           onto an ALREADY-INSERTED fixture (NOT(ISNEW()) making it a change, not a create) would
           now be refused by this rule for the first time. Sweep owed, not performed here.

        FLS: unaffected - this is a validation rule, not a field grant.

        Risk: MEDIUM - the custom permission is a new dependency this rule cannot function
        correctly without. The stage boundary itself is NOT a judgement call left open here; it
        is a settled user decision (Gate 1, 2026-08-31) - see the LOCK BOUNDARY block above.
    -->
    <fullName>Record_Type_Is_Immutable</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>A disposition&apos;s record type cannot change once BOV Outreach or later stages begin - the principal already approved a specific path at the sale-decision approval, whose entry criterion is Disposition Readiness.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    NOT(ISNEW()),
    ISCHANGED(RecordTypeId),
    NOT(ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Disposition Readiness&apos;)),
    NOT($Permission.Disposition_Record_Type_Override)
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Disposition_Stage__c</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>This disposition&apos;s record type cannot be changed once the sale-decision approval has run. The principal already approved a specific on-market or off-market path. Contact a system administrator if this was filed under the wrong path.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
